{"term":"depart","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:3ea6360611bc5bdf12","definition":"To leave.","example":"[…] he that hath no ſtomacke to this feaſt,\nLet him depart, […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["leave"],"antonyms":["arrive","come","stay","live","conform"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["departee","departer","depart with"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depart#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:597d733ea9725b9b80","definition":"To set out on a journey.","example":"And soo she receyued hym vpon suffysaunt seurte / so alle her hurtes were wel restored of al that she coude complayne / and thenne he departed vnto the Courte of kyne Arthur / and there openly the reed knyghte of the reed laundes putte hym in the mercy of syre Launcelot and syr Gawayne","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["arrive","come","stay","live","conform"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["departee","departer","depart with"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depart#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:52910243e379b8cc9c","definition":"To die.","example":"[…] his Tongue,\nSounds euer after as a ſullen Bell\nRemembred, knolling a departing Friend.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["die"],"antonyms":["arrive","come","stay","live","conform"],"collocations":[],"usage":"euphemistic","register":"euphemistic, intransitive","wordFamily":["departee","departer","depart with"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depart#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:aca7403774c8301b8e","definition":"To disappear, vanish; to cease to exist.","example":"For youth departs, and pleasure flies,\nAnd life consumes away,","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["arrive","come","stay","live","conform"],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["departee","departer","depart with"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depart#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:47002a0500c00293de","definition":"To deviate (from), be different (from), fail to conform.","example":"His latest statements seemed to depart from party policy somewhat.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["deviate","digress","diverge","sidetrack","straggle","vary"],"antonyms":["arrive","come","stay","live","conform"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["departee","departer","depart with"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depart#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9028544905c5305199","definition":"To go away from; to leave.","example":"[...] he [...] did pray them only to do no thing against the honor of God, & rather to depart the territories of his empire, then to suffer their consciences to be forced.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["leave"],"antonyms":["arrive","come","stay","live","conform"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["departee","departer","depart with"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depart#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c7079541e029c6a218","definition":"To lose control of an aircraft; to \"depart\" (sense 5) from controlled flight (with the aircraft as the direct object)","example":"The envelope protection system allows the pilot to maneuver at high angles of attack without the risk of departing the airplane","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["arrive","come","stay","live","conform"],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":["departee","departer","depart with"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depart#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2092938dfad22a2baa","definition":"To divide up; to distribute, share.","example":"and so all the worlde seythe that betwyxte three knyghtes is departed clerely knyghthode, that is Sir Launcelot du Lake, Sir Trystrams de Lyones and Sir Lamerok de Galys—thes bere now the renowne.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["arrive","come","stay","live","conform"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["departee","departer","depart with"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depart#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3a8326768bdd9dda51","definition":"To separate, part.","example":"Syr knyght[,] said the two squyers that were with her[,] yonder are two knyghtes that fyghte for thys lady, goo thyder and departe them[…].","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["arrive","come","stay","live","conform"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["departee","departer","depart with"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depart#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c90b6e66c62ab6f855","definition":"Division; separation, as of compound substances.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["departee","departer","depart with"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depart#Eng